  "lessons": [
    "Removing objects from the approved full scene produced a clean independent sky and sea layer while retaining the horizon and palette.",
    "Explicit full-frame uniform resizing is appropriate for this opaque background; it does not normalize a silhouette or crop painted content.",
    "Shadow v1 retained cleaner exterior alpha than the attempted narrow contour correction. The revision increased the contaminated bounds instead of tightening them.",
    "The selected shadow peaks at alpha 133, above the requested 25-30% opacity. Preserve the measured source and judge the actual composed result rather than claiming the prompt guarantees opacity.",
    "A fixed 0.235 shadow scale preserves the full meaningful contour with its original guide center and upper-contact anchor. This is a static design choice, not a bounds-derived transform.",
    "Use the corresponding original phase as the first reference for every wave. These three images use no generated wave ancestor and share one center registration.",
    "Frame 006 exceeded the initial 0.25 window by a quarter HD pixel on each side. One common 0.249 scale keeps the complete center family inside without per-phase fitting or clipping meaningful foam.",
    "Keep sand and solid ocean fill out of the independent foam sprites. The corrected runtime wave compositor restores its clean base before rendering the current wave families.",
    "Alpha 1-7 exterior residue remains in raw transparent sprites; numerical alpha and colored composites distinguish it from real visible background contamination."
  ],
